// Data Sync ETL Hub case study.
//
// Source: the code itself. There is no written playbook for this project, so
// every claim below was traced through the repository at Desktop/DF-JS-ETL
// (86 commits, Dec 2025 to Aug 2026), the live share at Desktop/FTP_Share, and
// a targeted read of the client's Salesforce org retrieve.
//
// The client is anonymised throughout. Search this file for "manufacturer"
// before publishing if that ever needs to change.
//
// Honesty constraints agreed before writing:
//   - The system ran in UAT. It was never carried production volume. No uptime,
//     throughput or incident numbers appear anywhere on this page.
//   - The commits are design corrections found during build, not outage
//     post-mortems, and are described that way.
//   - Where ARCHITECTURE.md and the code disagree, both are stated. See the
//     "Doc vs Code" tab. Nothing is silently merged.
//   - Salesforce claims are limited to what the org retrieve actually proves.
//     The retrieve is old and partial, so absence is recorded as unknown rather
//     than as "does not exist".
//
// Block shapes are documented in ../eudoro/index.js.

